        "checkedAt": "2026-10-13T06:36:14.963Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Each domain (SageMaker AI domain Team A and SageMaker AI domain Team B) provides a dedicated Amazon SageMaker Studio GUI and is configured with a team-specific execution role ( TeamA-role and TeamB-role respectively).",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/share-gpu-clusters-across-teams-with-isolation-and-fairness-using-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-08T16:20:04.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-13T06:36:14.963Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Within each namespace, teams can run their own HyperPod Spaces (interactive development environments), HyperPod PyTorch jobs (distributed training workloads), and HyperPod Inference endpoints (model serving).",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/share-gpu-clusters-across-teams-with-isolation-and-fairness-using-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-08T16:20:04.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-13T06:36:14.963Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The first is a POSIX-compliant file system (Amazon FSx for Lustre or Amazon FSx for OpenZFS) organized into per-team shared directories ( /fsx/TeamA , /fsx/TeamB ) and per-user home directories ( /home/User1 , /home/User2 ).",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/share-gpu-clusters-across-teams-with-isolation-and-fairness-using-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
